    failure: 'Voice references fail when they become lists of fashionable words to add or ban without context. They also fail when every article uses the same opening, number of sections, example cadence, and conclusion. Consistency should help readers recognize judgment and boundaries, not make distinct topics sound mechanically interchangeable.',
